  "details": "Malicious package. Impersonates the `base-x` encoding library (homepage pointing at cryptocoinjs/base-x, identical layout). The exported `decode(string)` in both `src/esm/index.js` and `src/cjs/index.cjs` is patched with obfuscator.io-style code that POSTs every caller-supplied input, typically a base58-encoded private key or address, to a hardcoded Telegram bot (`sendMessage` with `{chat_id, text: string}`): bot 8444411730 in early versions and bot 8040141601 in 0.0.4. Same technique as `base62-86x` (MAL-2026-6446). Versions 0.0.1 to 0.0.4 were verified from their source; a 0.0.5 was also published on 2025-08-04. Unpublished from npm on 2025-09-11.",
